      "originalPrompt": "REPLICATE the reference image's LAYOUT, COMPOSITION, TYPOGRAPHY STYLE, COLOR SCHEME, and DESIGN APPROACH. ADAPT the visual context to pest control: replace ALL skincare-specific visual elements with pest-control relevant visuals. Replace the brand name with 'Bugo' and all text with English, left-aligned (LTR).\n\nBACKGROUND: Soft warm beige gradient background (#F5E6D3 to #E8D5C4), clean and neutral. NO skincare elements, NO body parts, NO cosmetic textures.\n\nLAYOUT: Split-screen vertical comparison format, two equal sections side by side with clear division line.\n\nLEFT SECTION (Day 1):\nTOP LABEL: \"Day 1\" - white text, bold sans-serif font, positioned in upper left corner with subtle drop shadow\nVISUAL: Indoor room corner showing pest problem - small cockroach silhouettes (#4A4A4A) scattered on light wooden floor, few ant trails visible along baseboard, suggesting active pest presence. Clean, realistic home interior background.\n\nRIGHT SECTION (Day 7):\nTOP LABEL: \"Day 7\" - white text, bold sans-serif font, positioned in upper right corner with subtle drop shadow  \nVISUAL: Same room corner completely pest-free - clean light wooden floor, no insects visible, peaceful and pristine home environment. Same interior style as left side for consistency.\n\nPRODUCT (center-bottom): REMOVE the original skincare bottle COMPLETELY. In its exact position, place the Bugo device: white oval/egg-shaped ultrasonic pest repeller with blue LED glow from the bottom rim (#2196F3), 'Bugo' text in gray on the device face. The user will upload the actual Bugo product photo as a second reference image — use that exact product image.\n\nBRAND TEXT (on device): \"Bugo\" - clean gray sans-serif text on the device face, centered\n\nPRODUCT TYPE (below device): \"ULTRASONIC\" - bold black uppercase letters, same font weight and style as original\n\nPRODUCT DESCRIPTION (below product type): \"PEST REPELLER\" - black uppercase letters, slightly smaller than product type text\n\nLIGHTING: Soft, even lighting throughout both sections, warm tone matching the beige color scheme\n\nASPECT RATIO: 1:1\n\nKeep the same layout and element positions. You MUST replace any visual elements specific to the original niche (skincare, body parts, cosmetic textures) with pest-control or clean-home relevant visuals. DO NOT keep niche-irrelevant imagery. The transformation should show pest presence to pest elimination, maintaining the same dramatic before/after impact as the reference.",
