      "angle": "chemical-free safety for families",
      "folderId": "root",
      "originalPrompt": "REPLICATE the reference image's LAYOUT, COMPOSITION, TYPOGRAPHY STYLE, COLOR SCHEME, and DESIGN APPROACH. ADAPT all visual content to pest control — no traces of the original respiratory/supplement niche.\n\nBACKGROUND: Light gray gradient background (#F5F5F5) typical of iOS Messages app interface.\n\nBRAND HEADER (top-center): Green gradient pill-shaped banner stretching across width. Left portion bright lime green (#8BC34A), right portion darker forest green (#4CAF50). White bold sans-serif text 'Bugo' with small white pest control icon (house with shield) to the left of text, all centered within the banner.\n\nMESSAGE CONVERSATION (vertical flow, alternating sides):\n\nMESSAGE 1 (left side): Light gray rounded speech bubble (#E5E5EA), black text in iOS system font: 'Stop wasting money on cheap pest repellers that don't work'\n\nMESSAGE 2 (right side): Blue iOS message bubble (#007AFF), white text: 'What do you mean? I'm using a $20 ultrasonic device for my roach problem'\n\nMESSAGE 3 (left side): Light gray rounded speech bubble (#E5E5EA), black text: 'We use dual-wave technology for real results. That's 5X more effective than basic ultrasonic devices'\n\nMESSAGE 4 (right side): Blue iOS message bubble (#007AFF), white text with emoji: 'WTF 😤 No one told me that'\n\nMESSAGE 5 (left side): Light gray rounded speech bubble (#E5E5EA), black text: 'Lol...just go to bugo.com and read the reviews. Sarah saw results in 3 days.'\n\niMESSAGE INTERFACE (bottom): Standard iOS messaging interface with gray camera icon, gray 'A' icon, white text input field with 'iMessage' placeholder text, and blue microphone icon on right.\n\nSpeech bubbles have standard iOS rounded corners and proper spacing between messages. Text uses iOS system font (San Francisco) with appropriate weights. Message timestamps and delivery indicators are NOT visible, matching the reference.\n\nASPECT RATIO: 1:1\n\nKeep the same layout and message flow structure. Replace all respiratory/supplement references with pest control equivalents. DO NOT add any visual elements not present in the original reference.",
